window.docContents[211].resolve({"/Browse-the-paper-and-supplement/#section-S-S___A":{"contents":"Whole-space supplement, lines 9632–11076.\n\n* Uniformly local tests and their interpretation* Confinement and trajectory assumptions* Weighted trajectory assumptions for the general comparison* Initial statistics in the uniformly local class* The whole-space linear comparison field* The confined finite-particle process* Entropy admissibility under confinement* The adjoint linearized flow on the whole space* Qualitative convergence on path space* Uniformly local spaces and transported cutoffs\n\n","context":"Fluctuations of Riesz gases\u0009Browse the paper and supplement","header":"3.23. S.A. Unconfined and general whole-space comparisons","id":"/Browse-the-paper-and-supplement/#section-S-S___A"},"/The-sharp-sub-Coulomb-commutator/#comm-lean-HRS___Commutator___Whole___subcoulomb_commutator":{"contents":"Let  be an integer and .There are , depending only on . Let  be real with . Let  be an integer and let  be pairwise distinct.When , assume .For , let  be Lipschitz withFor ,The quantity in parentheses is nonnegative. The mixed and background integrals defining  and  converge absolutely.The whole-space kernel is  for  and  for .Set . The energy and first transport commutator areThe integrals expand into the particle sum with  omitted, the mixed terms and the background term. All vector norms are Euclidean.In the transport bound,  denotes the Lipschitz seminorm. The componentwise distributional derivative  has multiplier  for the Fourier convention . Each fractional-derivative norm is the norm of a representative satisfying the distributional identity with absolutely convergent pairings against every complex Schwartz test function.\n\nVerification: Lean proof term available.\n\nSource: HRS/Commutator/Whole/Assembly.lean.\n\nDeclaration type, as written:\n\ntheorem subcoulomb_commutator (hd : 3 ≤ d) {s : ℝ} (hs0 : 0 ≤ s) (hsd : s < (d : ℝ) - 2) :\n    ∃ C C₀ : ℝ, 0 < C ∧ 0 < C₀ ∧ ∀ ρ : Euc d → ℝ, Integrable ρ → MemLp ρ ⊤ volume →\n      ∫ x, ρ x = 1 → (s = 0 → LogIntegrable ρ) →\n      ∀ (v : Euc d → Euc d) (K : ℝ), SubTransport d s v K →\n      ∀ (N : ℕ) (X : Fin N → Euc d), 1 ≤ N → Function.Injective X →\n        EnergyIntegrable s X ρ ∧ CommIntegrable s X ρ v ∧\n        0 ≤ modEnergy s X ρ - (if s = 0 then Real.log (lamN d N ρ) / (2 * (N : ℝ)) else 0) +\n              C₀ * normE ⊤ ρ * lamN d N ρ ^ ((d : ℝ) - s) ∧\n        |commA s X ρ v| ≤ C * K *\n          (modEnergy s X ρ - (if s = 0 then Real.log (lamN d N ρ) / (2 * (N : ℝ)) else 0) +\n            C₀ * normE ⊤ ρ * lamN d N ρ ^ ((d : ℝ) - s))\n\n\nInspected Lean proof body:\n\nby\n  obtain ⟨C, hC, S⟩ := subcoulomb_commutator_scale hd hs0 hsd\n  obtain ⟨Cp, hCp, S'⟩ := S ⊤ (by simp)\n  refine ⟨C, 2 * Cp, hC, by positivity, fun ρ h1 hinf hmass hlog v K hv N X hN hX => ?_⟩\n  have hM := normE_top_pos ρ h1 hinf hmass\n  have hNpos : (0 : ℝ) < N := by exact_mod_cast hN\n  have hd0 : (d : ℝ) ≠ 0 := by\n    have : (3 : ℝ) ≤ d := by exact_mod_cast hd\n    linarith\n  have hNM : 0 < (N : ℝ) * normE ⊤ ρ := mul_pos hNpos hM\n  have hlam : 0 < lamN d N ρ := Real.rpow_pos_of_pos hNM _\n  have hlamd : lamN d N ρ ^ (d : ℝ) = ((N : ℝ) * normE ⊤ ρ)⁻¹ := by\n    unfold lamN\n    rw [← Real.rpow_mul hNM.le, show (-(1 : ℝ) / d) * d = -1 by field_simp, Real.rpow_neg_one]\n  have hkey : lamN d N ρ ^ (-s) / (N : ℝ) = normE ⊤ ρ * lamN d N ρ ^ ((d : ℝ) - s) := by\n    rw [sub_eq_add_neg, Real.rpow_add hlam, hlamd]\n    field_simp\n  obtain ⟨hE, hCI, hQ, hA⟩ := S' ρ h1 hinf hmass hlog v K hv N X hN hX (lamN d N ρ) hlam\n  have hQe : scaleQ s Cp ⊤ (lamN d N ρ) X ρ =\n      modEnergy s X ρ - (if s = 0 then Real.log (lamN d N ρ) / (2 * (N : ℝ)) else 0) +\n        2 * Cp * normE ⊤ ρ * lamN d N ρ ^ ((d : ℝ) - s) := by\n    unfold scaleQ\n    simp only [ENNReal.inv_top, ENNReal.toReal_zero, sub_zero, mul_one]\n    rw [hkey]\n    ring\n  rw [hQe] at hQ hA\n  exact ⟨hE, hCI, hQ, hA⟩\n\n\n","context":"Fluctuations of Riesz gases\u0009The sharp sub-Coulomb commutator\u0009Lean declarations and evidence","header":"1.6.3. Whole space · sharp-scale theorem","id":"/The-sharp-sub-Coulomb-commutator/#comm-lean-HRS___Commutator___Whole___subcoulomb_commutator"}});